1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,148
Worked example twelve point one.

2
00:00:02,148 --> 00:00:08,710
Five carbons must be split around the oxygen, either one plus four, or two plus three.

3
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:16,341
One plus four gives the methoxybutanes, and a butyl group has four arrangements, so four ethers.

4
00:00:16,341 --> 00:00:21,744
Two plus three gives the ethoxypropanes, with two arrangements of propyl.

5
00:00:21,744 --> 00:00:23,216
Six ethers in all.

6
00:00:23,216 --> 00:00:28,398
Any methoxybutane with any ethoxypropane is a pair of metamers.

